Propose decomposition step {{ step_number }}: undo one semantic transformation
while preserving the operator contract. First identify mechanisms actually present
in the current kernel. Remove dependent mechanisms before their prerequisites;
never invent a fixed sequence or split parameter tuning into repeated skills.
One transformation may include necessary layout and thread-mapping changes.

Return exactly one JSON object. If no meaningful simplification remains, return
{"done": true, "reason": "code evidence showing no remaining optimization"}.
Do not call budget exhaustion a naive kernel. Otherwise write the complete
simplified kernel to output_path and return done=false, action_category, locus,
backward_edit, before_features, and after_features. Each feature is {locus, name};
before means the simpler predecessor, after means the current kernel. Inventory
all optimization mechanisms across loci; remove one at the declared locus.
These are claims for independent
verification, not validated state. Do not claim validation or performance results.

